			"1": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "FREQUENCY & UNIPOLARITY\n\nOscillators will oscillate between their positive and negative amplitude.\nThe oscillation speed is controlled by the frequency and is measured in Hertz.\n\nAssignment: expose the frequency of the sine node and crank up the value.\n\nOscillators can be made unipolar in the node panel.\nThis means that they will only produce positive or negative values, depending on the frequency.\n\nAssignment: set the Sine node to unipolar (check the node panel) and play around with polarity of the frequency."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 563,
					"width": 915.676513671875,
					"x": 173.92181396484375,
					"y": 349.35626220703125
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
