					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "OSCILLATORS\n\nOscillators are a category of nodes that produce oscillating float values.\nThese values are amazing for modulating parameters, generating texturing, animation and breathing life into static movements.\n\nIn this tutorial we'll go over the parameters found on the oscillator nodes and how to use them.\nWe'll also provide two of examples that use oscillators in practical applications."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 178,
					"width": 915.02288818359375,
					"x": 173.921905517578125,
					"y": 117.76116943359375
