					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "AMPLITUDE & OFFSET\n\nAmplitude dictates the range of values that an oscillator can produce.\n\nAssignment: expose the amplitude of the sine node and make the circle move out of the screen.\n\nOffset is a value added to the output of the oscillator.\nCombining amplitude, offset and unipolarity allows you to get every imaginable range.\n\nAssignment: make the circle oscillate between 0.5 and 0.8 using amplitude, offset and unipolarity."
					}
				},
